          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-862",
              "name": "Broken Function Level Authorization and IDOR in /api/sales/[id]/cancel",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Broken Function Level Authorization and IDOR in /api/sales/[id]/cancel"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The sales invoice cancellation endpoint does not enforce role-based access control or tenant isolation, allowing low-privilege counter billers to cancel any sales invoice across the system."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The sales invoice cancellation endpoint does not enforce role-based access control or tenant isolation, allowing low-privilege counter billers to cancel any sales invoice across the system.\n\nAn authenticated attacker with the low-privilege `biller` role can cancel arbitrary confirmed sales invoices without administrative authorization. Cancelling an invoice restores inventory batch quantities, creates adjustment stock events, updates outbox synchronization, and alters statutory audit logs without store owner approval.\n\nIn `src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts`, verify that `locals.user.role === 'owner_admin'`. If not, return a 403 Forbidden response. Additionally, ensure the sale belongs to the user's `storeId` before executing the cancellation.",
                "markdown": "The sales invoice cancellation endpoint does not enforce role-based access control or tenant isolation, allowing low-privilege counter billers to cancel any sales invoice across the system.\n\nAn authenticated attacker with the low-privilege `biller` role can cancel arbitrary confirmed sales invoices without administrative authorization. Cancelling an invoice restores inventory batch quantities, creates adjustment stock events, updates outbox synchronization, and alters statutory audit logs without store owner approval.\n\nIn `src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts`, verify that `locals.user.role === 'owner_admin'`. If not, return a 403 Forbidden response. Additionally, ensure the sale belongs to the user's `storeId` before executing the cancellation."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-862",
                  "stride:E"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/862.html"
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-200",
              "name": "CVE-2026-92708 in devalue 5.9.1 (Process Memory Disclosure)",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-92708 in devalue 5.9.1 (Process Memory Disclosure)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Svelte devalue versions 5.1.0 through 5.9.2 contain a cross-request process memory disclosure vulnerability where stringify and uneval serialize a typed array by emitting its entire backing ArrayBuffer rather than the slice view. When serializing a Node Buffer sharing a process-wide pool, up to 64 KB of uninitialized or unrelated process memory may be leaked."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Svelte devalue versions 5.1.0 through 5.9.2 contain a cross-request process memory disclosure vulnerability where stringify and uneval serialize a typed array by emitting its entire backing ArrayBuffer rather than the slice view. When serializing a Node Buffer sharing a process-wide pool, up to 64 KB of uninitialized or unrelated process memory may be leaked.\n\nIn vulnerable configurations returning Node Buffers in SSR load() functions, up to 64 KB of shared memory from other concurrent requests could be leaked in rendered HTML responses. In this codebase, devalue is not directly imported.\n\nRun `npm update devalue` or update `@sveltejs/kit` to ensure `devalue` resolves to `>= 5.9.3`.",
                "markdown": "Svelte devalue versions 5.1.0 through 5.9.2 contain a cross-request process memory disclosure vulnerability where stringify and uneval serialize a typed array by emitting its entire backing ArrayBuffer rather than the slice view. When serializing a Node Buffer sharing a process-wide pool, up to 64 KB of uninitialized or unrelated process memory may be leaked.\n\nIn vulnerable configurations returning Node Buffers in SSR load() functions, up to 64 KB of shared memory from other concurrent requests could be leaked in rendered HTML responses. In this codebase, devalue is not directly imported.\n\nRun `npm update devalue` or update `@sveltejs/kit` to ensure `devalue` resolves to `>= 5.9.3`."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "0.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
