      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Broken Function Level Authorization and IDOR in /api/sales/[id]/cancel\n\nThe sales invoice cancellation endpoint does not enforce role-based access control or tenant isolation, allowing low-privilege counter billers to cancel any sales invoice across the system."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 4,
                  "endLine": 11,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export async function POST({ params, locals }) {\n\tif (!locals.user) {\n\t\treturn new Response('Unauthorized', { status: 401 });\n\t}\n\n\tconst sale = await salesService.cancelSale(params.id);\n\treturn json(sale);\n}"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Enforce owner_admin role check on sales cancellation"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/sales/[id]/cancel",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 4,
                        "endLine": 11
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "export async function POST({ params, locals }) {\n\tif (!locals.user) {\n\t\treturn new Response('Unauthorized', { status: 401 });\n\t}\n\n\tif (locals.user.role !== 'owner_admin') {\n\t\treturn new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Forbidden: Admin role required' }), {\n\t\t\tstatus: 403,\n\t\t\theaders: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }\n\t\t});\n\t}\n\n\tconst sale = await salesService.cancelSale(params.id);\n\treturn json(sale);\n}"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "In `src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts`, verify that `locals.user.role === 'owner_admin'`. If not, return a 403 Forbidden response. Additionally, ensure the sale belongs to the user's `storeId` before executing the cancellation.",
                "markdown": "In `src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts`, verify that `locals.user.role === 'owner_admin'`. If not, return a 403 Forbidden response. Additionally, ensure the sale belongs to the user's `storeId` before executing the cancellation."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "14dbe49491a884ad6fd63864f4cb642039dcfeb6e21000e7467c15ade07b9463"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "6.5",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "3174e38e6c72ef9ffcecc7abfdfb44ac425908b43bf07eeb479e0aacf5dcaf79",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0001",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 6.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-11-01 13:02:27 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:5173",
              "endpoint": "/api/sales/[id]/cancel",
              "method": "POST",
              "cwe": "CWE-862",
              "impact": "An authenticated attacker with the low-privilege `biller` role can cancel arbitrary confirmed sales invoices without administrative authorization. Cancelling an invoice restores inventory batch quantities, creates adjustment stock events, updates outbox synchronization, and alters statutory audit logs without store owner approval.",
              "technical_analysis": "In `src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts`:\nThe handler only verifies that a session exists (`if (!locals.user)`). Unlike `src/routes/api/purchases/[id]/cancel/+server.ts`, which restricts cancellation to `owner_admin`, `src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts` completely omits any role check. Furthermore, neither the route handler nor `salesService.cancelSale(params.id)` validates that the target invoice belongs to the caller's store (`sale.storeId === locals.user.storeId`). Consequently, any biller can cancel any sale by ID.\n\nWhen `cancelSale` executes, `DbSaleRepository.updateStatus` marks the invoice as `'cancelled'`, restores batch stock quantities in `batchesTable`, inserts adjustment records in `batchStockEventsTable`, logs sync events in `syncOutboxTable`, and records a cancellation entry in `auditLogTable`.",
              "remediation_steps": "In `src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts`, verify that `locals.user.role === 'owner_admin'`. If not, return a 403 Forbidden response. Additionally, ensure the sale belongs to the user's `storeId` before executing the cancellation.",
              "counterevidence": "Checked whether hooks.server.ts or salesService enforces role restrictions on sales cancellation. Confirmed that hooks.server.ts only validates session existence, and neither the route handler nor DbSaleRepository.updateStatus validates role or tenant ownership. Dynamically executed cancellation using the biller account and confirmed invoice cancellation, stock restoration, and audit log mutation.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If counter billers were granted explicit business authority to void retail tickets under store policy, severity would decrease to Medium; however, missing multi-tenant storeId validation still allows unauthorized cross-tenant cancellation.",
              "fix_verification": "Gate 1 (Applicability): Verified line numbers 4-11 match verbatim in src/routes/api/sales/[id]/cancel/+server.ts.\nGate 2 (Security closure): With the check added, requests from biller receive HTTP 403 Forbidden before salesService.cancelSale is reached.\nGate 3 (Bypass review): Mirrors the working authorization guard in src/routes/api/purchases/[id]/cancel/+server.ts.\nGate 4 (Preserved behavior): Administrative users (owner_admin) can still cancel sales invoices as expected.\nGate 5 (Repository checks): Syntactically valid TypeScript matching SvelteKit RequestHandler convention.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Log in as an administrator (owner_admin) and create a sales invoice via `POST /api/sales`.\n2. Note the generated invoice ID (e.g. `88aac12a-89c2-45e0-a8d7-4c86a3c8df3d`).\n3. Log in as a low-privilege counter biller (`role: biller`) to obtain a biller session cookie.\n4. Send a `POST` request to `/api/sales/<sale_id>/cancel` using the biller's session cookie.\n5. Observe that the server returns HTTP 200 OK with the sale status updated to `cancelled`, and batch stock restored.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Broken Function Level Authorization in /api/sync/push Allows Arbitrary Database Manipulation\n\nThe database synchronization push endpoint allows low-privilege counter billers to insert, update, and delete arbitrary records across transactional and master database tables, bypassing application authorization controls."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/routes/api/sync/push/+server.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 24,
                  "endLine": 28,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export const POST: RequestHandler = async ({ request, locals }) => {\n\tif (!locals.user) {\n\t\treturn json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 });\n\t}\n\n\tconst body = await request.json();"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Enforce owner_admin role check on sync push endpoint"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/sync/push",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "src/routes/api/sync/push/+server.ts"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 24,
                        "endLine": 28
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "export const POST: RequestHandler = async ({ request, locals }) => {\n\tif (!locals.user) {\n\t\treturn json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 });\n\t}\n\n\tif (locals.user.role !== 'owner_admin') {\n\t\treturn json({ error: 'Forbidden: Admin role required for database sync operations' }, { status: 403 });\n\t}\n\n\tconst body = await request.json();"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "Restrict `POST /api/sync/push` to `owner_admin` or a dedicated system sync token:\n```typescript\nif (locals.user.role !== 'owner_admin') {\n    return json({ error: 'Forbidden: Admin role required' }, { status: 403 });\n}\n```",
                "markdown": "Restrict `POST /api/sync/push` to `owner_admin` or a dedicated system sync token:\n```typescript\nif (locals.user.role !== 'owner_admin') {\n    return json({ error: 'Forbidden: Admin role required' }, { status: 403 });\n}\n```"
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "34869b57030014b2918dcba1d550d8e00baeaa88c025a925f73f53006f2cb0d1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "7.1",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "d7c920010c9f23b94628a4bff3313ffa3e22ab46a013b2f4cf84bc58c51bf50c",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0002",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.1,
              "timestamp": "2026-11-01 13:02:58 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:5173",
              "endpoint": "/api/sync/push",
              "method": "POST",
              "cwe": "CWE-862",
              "impact": "A counter biller, restricted from editing products, supplier balances, batches, or deleting transactions through standard UI and API routes, can craft arbitrary sync events via `/api/sync/push` to insert, overwrite, or delete master products, batches, stock event deltas, customer balances, supplier balances, and purchase orders directly in the database.",
              "technical_analysis": "In `src/routes/api/sync/push/+server.ts`:\nThe endpoint is intended for store server to cloud synchronization. However, it only requires `if (!locals.user) { return json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 }); }` without verifying user roles.\nAny authenticated user (such as a counter biller) can send raw sync entries affecting:\n- `products`\n- `product_units`\n- `batches`\n- `batch_stock_events`\n- `suppliers`\n- `customers`\n- `purchases`\n- `purchase_items`\n- `sales`\n- `sale_items`\n- `payments`\n- `returns`\n- `return_items`\n\nThe handler executes a direct database transaction applying `insert`, `update`, or `delete` on the corresponding table or applying stock adjustments to `batchesTable`. This allows complete bypass of application-level business constraints and role authorization.",
              "remediation_steps": "Restrict `POST /api/sync/push` to `owner_admin` or a dedicated system sync token:\n```typescript\nif (locals.user.role !== 'owner_admin') {\n    return json({ error: 'Forbidden: Admin role required' }, { status: 403 });\n}\n```",
              "counterevidence": "Checked if any gateway or hook limits access to /api/sync/push. Confirmed that hooks.server.ts permits any authenticated user. Examined POST /api/sync/push and confirmed it only requires locals.user without role validation. Tested dynamically by injecting and deleting a product record using the biller session cookie, and confirmed direct database modification.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If the endpoint was unauthenticated, severity would increase to High/Critical; since authentication as a valid user is required, severity is High.",
              "fix_verification": "Gate 1 (Applicability): Verified line numbers 24-28 in src/routes/api/sync/push/+server.ts match verbatim.\nGate 2 (Security closure): With the check added, requests from biller receive HTTP 403 Forbidden before any database transaction is initiated.\nGate 3 (Bypass review): All operation types (insert, update, delete) across all tableMap entities are protected by this single entrypoint gate.\nGate 4 (Preserved behavior): Store server synchronization processes running with administrator credentials or appropriate sync credentials can still push sync events.\nGate 5 (Repository checks): Syntactically valid TypeScript matching SvelteKit RequestHandler convention.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Log in as a low-privilege counter biller (`role: biller`) to obtain a valid session cookie.\n2. Send a `POST` request to `/api/sync/push` with a crafted `SyncOutboxEntry` inserting a new product or modifying an existing batch.\n3. Observe that the server returns HTTP 200 OK with `status: \"ok\"`.\n4. Verify by querying `GET /api/products/<injected_id>` that the product was directly inserted into the store database.\n5. Send a `POST` request to `/api/sync/push` with operation `'delete'` to verify deletion.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
