            "security-severity": "6.5",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "d7c920010c9f23b94628a4bff3313ffa3e22ab46a013b2f4cf84bc58c51bf50c",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0003",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 6.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-11-01 13:03:21 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:5173",
              "endpoint": "/api/sync/pull",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-862",
              "impact": "Low-privilege counter staff can harvest raw business event data queued for cloud sync, including internal batch updates, sales records, customer identifiers, supplier transaction details, and audit metadata.",
              "technical_analysis": "In `src/routes/api/sync/pull/+server.ts`:\nThe handler defines `export const GET: RequestHandler = async ({ url }) => { ... }`. It does not check `locals.user.role`.\nThe query filters `syncOutboxTable` by `targetNode = callerNode`. By supplying `?clientId=cloud` or `?clientId=store_server`, any authenticated caller can query and receive all outbox records, exposing raw database row payloads across multiple domain tables (`sales`, `batches`, `batch_stock_events`, `suppliers`, etc.).",
              "remediation_steps": "In `src/routes/api/sync/pull/+server.ts`, restrict access to `owner_admin` or a dedicated synchronization credential:\n```typescript\nif (!locals.user || locals.user.role !== 'owner_admin') {\n    return json({ error: 'Forbidden: Admin role required' }, { status: 403 });\n}\n```",
              "counterevidence": "Checked if /api/sync/pull restricts callers. While hooks.server.ts ensures session authentication, the route handler GET in src/routes/api/sync/pull/+server.ts completely lacks any role check. By passing ?clientId=cloud, any low-privilege biller can dump synchronization outbox records containing transactions, batches, products, and customer details.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If unauthenticated access were possible, severity would be High; since authentication is required, severity is Medium.",
              "fix_verification": "Gate 1 (Applicability): Verified line numbers 7-8 match verbatim in src/routes/api/sync/pull/+server.ts.\nGate 2 (Security closure): With the check added, requests from biller receive HTTP 403 Forbidden and no outbox rows are queried or leaked.\nGate 3 (Bypass review): Ensures both store_server and cloud targetNode pull queries are protected.\nGate 4 (Preserved behavior): System administration and authorized sync services can still pull sync events.\nGate 5 (Repository checks): Syntactically valid TypeScript matching SvelteKit RequestHandler convention.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Log in as a low-privilege counter biller (`role: biller`).\n2. Send a `GET` request to `/api/sync/pull?clientId=cloud`.\n3. Observe that the server returns HTTP 200 OK with all queued replication items across the store.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
