          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "CVE-2026-92708 in devalue 5.9.1 (Process Memory Disclosure)\n\nSvelte devalue versions 5.1.0 through 5.9.2 contain a cross-request process memory disclosure vulnerability where stringify and uneval serialize a typed array by emitting its entire backing ArrayBuffer rather than the slice view. When serializing a Node Buffer sharing a process-wide pool, up to 64 KB of uninitialized or unrelated process memory may be leaked."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
